> {dahinai} = real. {dahi} = real or imaginary. "Real" means "real in the
> universe of discourse". "Imaginary" means "not real in the universe of
> discourse".

Note that "xanri" does not mean "imaginary" in this sense, due to its x2;
for something to be "imaginary" in the Lojban sense, there must exist an
imaginer.

